  "notes": [
    "Formed flange lengths are outside dimensions: the published flat minimum (from the bend centre line) equals flange90 - (R + T) + BA90/2, checked for every published row.",
    "5052 Aluminum .080: the processing chart lists R = .045 but the bend table lists .038; .038 is the value consistent with its K and BD90, so it is used here.",
    "K is printed to two decimals and on a few rows disagrees with BD90 (BD90 = 2(R + T) - (pi/2)(R + K T) is off by more than .003 in for 5052 Aluminum .063, Brass .187 and .250, Titanium Grade 2 .040; re-read on 2026-11-09, the page does print these values). qfold.shops uses the K that reproduces BD90, since the bend deduction is what lays out the flat pattern, and keeps the printed K beside it."
  ],
